    "project": "research/statement_binding_audit_20261114/lean",
    "theorem": "StatementBindingAudit.header_binding_controls_certificate",
    "statement": "theorem header_binding_controls_certificate : (∀ n : ℤ, 0 ≤ abs n) ∧ (∀ n : ℕ, namedArgument n=n) ∧ (¬ Function.Injective (prefixBefore barDelimiter)) ∧ (¬ Function.Injective (prefixBefore namedDelimiter)) ∧ (¬ Function.Injective (prefixBefore proofDelimiter)) ∧ (barSourceA ≠ barSourceB ∧ prefixBefore barDelimiter barSourceA=prefixBefore barDelimiter barSourceB) ∧ (namedSourceA ≠ namedSourceB ∧ prefixBefore namedDelimiter namedSourceA=prefixBefore namedDelimiter namedSourceB) ∧ (proofSourceA ≠ proofSourceB ∧ prefixBefore proofDelimiter proofSourceA=prefixBefore proofDelimiter proofSourceB)",
    "decl_sha256": "b3e3af513d61f8acbcfbca85f672699b2b8132900fdbe18a09c0208ea39c1988",
    "scope": "Kernel-checked genuine integer absolute-value/named-argument semantic controls and explicit transparent List-Char delimiter-prefix model. For each of the three fixed delimiter constants, concrete unequal source strings have the same model prefix, and the model prefix function is not injective. Genuine default-proof/inline-by/comment/string Lean declarations also compile under standard foundations/default settings. This is a delimiter-only model, not a formal refinement of Python regex, native parser/auditor, SHA256, every Lean syntax form, theorem semantics or execution authenticity. Native bounded written-header observations are separately archived procedural evidence and are not established by this theorem. No holes/custom axioms/native proof evaluation/unsafe initializer calls/raised limits/global flags/waivers/new cryptographic experiment/paid compute/upload.",
